-- title:
--   Gauss reduction maps the j-charts onto the Igusa charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $M\neq 0$, $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under `coeffEmb L`, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ that is an $A$-algebra, and let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm k M`, i.e. a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral $q$-expansion in `PowerSeries ℤ` whose associated series over $k$ is nonzero. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that: the Laurent expansion of $\sigma j$ is `coeffEmb L (qExpand ℚ p jq)` (that is, $j(q^p)$); $\sigma$ preserves the chart subalgebra `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` in both directions; and for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ whose members are exactly the $f$ with $f\cdot y(q)=x(q)$ in $L((q))$ for some $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ (the Gauss ring), the pullback $\sigma^{-1}(W_0)$ differs from $W_0$ and contains $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P\in A[X]$ of nonzero reduction. The conclusion asserts the existence of an element $t$ of the Igusa function field `igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w` (the Igusa function field attached to $k(X_1(M))\subseteq k((q))$ and the Hasse-invariant root function of $w$) and of $k$-algebra homomorphisms $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}:k\otimes_A \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j\to \mathrm{chartRing}\,k\,\{t\}$ and $\theta_\infty:k\otimes_A \mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j\to \mathrm{chartRing}\,k\,\{t^{-1}\}$, where $\mathrm{chartRing}\,k\,S$ denotes the elements of the Igusa function field integral over $k[S]$, such that: the Laurent expansion of $t$ is [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15); both maps are surjective; $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}(1\otimes j)=t^{p}$ and $\theta_\infty(1\otimes j^{-1})=t^{-p}$; whenever $b$, $b'$ lie in the finite and infinite charts with $b=b'\,j^{n}$ in $K$, one has $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}(1\otimes b)=\theta_\infty(1\otimes b')\,t^{pn}$; for $b$ in either chart and $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction and $\sigma(b)\cdot y(q)=x(q)$ in $L((q))$, the Laurent expansion of the image of $1\otimes b$ is $\bar x/\bar y$ in $k((q))$; and the kernel of each map is the ideal generated by the pure tensors $1\otimes b$ it contains.
--
--   This is the normality and identification statement for the second reduced component of the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_1(p)$: read through the level-$p$ involution $\sigma$, the reduction of the two integral $j$-charts maps onto the affine charts of the Igusa curve over $k$, with $j$ going to the $p$-th power of the reduced $j$-invariant. It strengthens the corresponding existence statement by surjectivity and by the description of the kernels, and is used in the construction of the pair of closed immersions from the special fibre of the two-chart integral model.
